From 5e2420e5e0c8d5034aa728965b04f1b11eb55adf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Gilbertson <880013+gilby@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 11:29:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep stock cutlass-dsl 4.6.0; fix the concurrency
 deadlock; 66.4 tok/s aggregate

Supersedes the 4.5.2 downgrade with a proper 4.6.0-compatible layer:

- thrmma_shim.py: PEP-562 lazy re-export of ThrMma/TiledMma back into
  cutlass.cute.core (4.6.0 moved them to the cutlass.cute top level)
- vllm_flash_attn/cute/utils.py overlay: pick the nvvm.fmax binding by
  signature feature-detection; cutlass-dsl 4.6.0 reports CUDA 12.9 in its
  toolchain metadata while shipping the new bindings, so the CUDA_VERSION
  proxy gate misfires
- apache-tvm-ffi 0.1.11 + tilelang 0.1.11: cutlass 4.6.0's tvm-ffi AOT
  provider needs make_kwargs_wrapper(map_dataclass_to_tuple=...) (>=0.1.10);
  tvm-ffi 0.1.12 aborts tilelang with a duplicate type-attr registration

Result: the batch>2 long-context decode deadlock that forced
--enforce-eager --max-num-seqs 2 is gone (fixed by the tvm-ffi 0.1.11
AOT-recompiled cutedsl kernels). PIECEWISE cudagraphs + --max-num-seqs 8
are fully stable: 48/48 benchmark turns with zero engine errors,
66.4 tok/s aggregate over 10 concurrent conversations (up from 28.6),
16.6 tok/s single-stream, quality parity held.

Remaining known issue (documented): FULL decode-graph replay of any capture
size desyncs NCCL between the two ranks (rank 1 c10::DistBackendError) --
collectives must stay uncaptured on the 2-node TP2 fabric, so PIECEWISE is
the supported graph mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
